---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro'
---

<Base title="Home">
  <h1>Welcome to Tech Class!</h1>
  <img
    src="/images/hero.webp"
    alt="Students working on their laptops"
    width="960"
    height="490"
    class="mt-6 h-auto w-full rounded-(--radius-card) shadow-md"
  />
  <p class="panel mt-8 text-lg sm:text-xl">
    Whether you're looking to build your basic computer skills for college and career success, or you're already
    tech-savvy and want to take your skills to the next level, we've got you covered. Earn certifications, build your
    résumé, and gain real-world confidence with every course.
  </p>

  <h2>Getting Started</h2>
  <p>
    Students are strongly encouraged to start with our <a href="/courses/digital-literacy">Digital Literacy</a> course.
    It covers basic computer skills that will provide a good foundation for any course moving forward, and it also
    gives us helpful information about your current capabilities.
  </p>
  <p>
    That said, if you consider yourself to be confidently tech-savvy you are welcome to skip the readings and test out
    of the course.
  </p>
  <p>
    To open course materials, create an account with the Register button at the top of the page. Your tech coach
    approves new accounts. Once you're approved, sign in on any computer and your progress comes with you.
  </p>

  <h2>Navigating Courses</h2>
  <p>
    Courses can be found on our <a href="/catalog">Course Catalog</a> page. Each course typically includes three units
    of material. Unit assignments include readings, videos, and activities to help you learn. When you finish
    something, press Mark complete at the bottom of it to go back to the course page, where you can see your progress.
    The Course Catalog shows your progress on every course, too.
  </p>
  <p>
    Each unit typically ends with a test or a project to assess your understanding. Tests are taken right here on the
    site. The exact expectation will vary based on individual skill levels, but a passing score is usually 90% or
    higher. Tests are open-note, and we are happy to offer any accommodations you may need. Don't stress!
  </p>
  <p>
    Your checkpoints, tests and projects go straight to your tech coach for grading, and your scores and feedback show
    up on the site. You're welcome to continue on to the next unit in the meantime.
  </p>

  <h2>Earning Certifications</h2>
  <p>
    Upon successfully completing each unit in a course, you'll receive an official NeuroDev certification.
    Certificates are awarded at tech ceremonies held every few months and represent all of your hard work.
  </p>
  <p>
    These certifications demonstrate valuable skills that you can showcase on your resume or job applications. Keep
    your certificates somewhere safe!
  </p>

  <h2>Contact Us</h2>
  <p>
    If you have any comments, questions, or concerns, please reach out to a tech coach in person or over email:
  </p>
  <div class="mt-4 grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2">
    <p class="panel mt-0">
      <strong>St. George, UT</strong><br />
      <a href="mailto:neurodevtechcoach@gmail.com">neurodevtechcoach@gmail.com</a><br />
      <a href="mailto:topher@neurodevmentoring.com">topher@neurodevmentoring.com</a>
    </p>
    <p class="panel mt-0">
      <strong>Raleigh, NC</strong><br />
      <a href="mailto:ethan@neurodevmentoring.com">ethan@neurodevmentoring.com</a>
    </p>
  </div>
</Base>
